# Apollo 14 near-surface model for AXISEM3D
#
# Vp: Mark & Sutton (1975), Apollo-14 adopted P-wave structure:
#      104 m/s from 0–8.0 m and 299 m/s below 8.0 m.
#      The 299 m/s value is carried to 84.5 m because a deeper
#      Apollo-14-specific lower boundary is not established here.
#
# Vs: Horvath et al. (1980) station-14 spectral-ratio model.
#      The detailed station-14 step values follow the preliminary
#      Horvath et al. (1979) LPSC Table 1 associated with the final
#      1980 journal study:
#      35, 70, 106, 141, 190, 222 and 250 m/s.
#      The discontinuities are modelling parameterisations and need
#      not be literal geological interfaces.
#
# Density: adopted Mark & Sutton-style comparison values:
#      1500 kg/m^3 from 0–8.0 m, 1700 kg/m^3 from 8.0–38.0 m,
#      and 1900 kg/m^3 below 38.0 m. These density values are included
#      as modelling inputs; they are not a standalone density profile
#      published by Mark & Sutton (1975).
#
# The model spans exactly 0–84.5 m. Depth is positive downward.

NAME        APOLLO14_MarkSuttonVp_HorvathStation14Vs_AdoptedDensity_0_to_84p5m
ANELASTIC   true
ANISOTROPIC false
UNITS       m
COLUMNS     depth vp vs rho qmu qkappa

    0.0000   104.0000     35.0000   1500.0    5000.0   1000000.0
    3.3000   104.0000     35.0000   1500.0    5000.0   1000000.0
    3.3000   104.0000     70.0000   1500.0    5000.0   1000000.0
    8.0000   104.0000     70.0000   1500.0    5000.0   1000000.0
    8.0000   299.0000     70.0000   1700.0    5000.0   1000000.0
   11.3000   299.0000     70.0000   1700.0    5000.0   1000000.0
   11.3000   299.0000    106.0000   1700.0    5000.0   1000000.0
   19.3000   299.0000    106.0000   1700.0    5000.0   1000000.0
   19.3000   299.0000    141.0000   1700.0    5000.0   1000000.0
   28.3000   299.0000    141.0000   1700.0    5000.0   1000000.0
   28.3000   299.0000    190.0000   1700.0    5000.0   1000000.0
   38.0000   299.0000    190.0000   1700.0    5000.0   1000000.0
   38.0000   299.0000    190.0000   1900.0    5000.0   1000000.0
   44.3000   299.0000    190.0000   1900.0    5000.0   1000000.0
   44.3000   299.0000    222.0000   1900.0    5000.0   1000000.0
   69.3000   299.0000    222.0000   1900.0    5000.0   1000000.0
   69.3000   299.0000    250.0000   1900.0    5000.0   1000000.0
   84.5000   299.0000    250.0000   1900.0    5000.0   1000000.0
